---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../content/site';
const contact = CONTACT_EMAIL || '[contact email to be added before launch]';
---

<Legal
  title={`Privacy policy | ${site.name}`}
  description={`How ${site.name}, a service by ${site.company}, handles personal information from visitors to this website.`}
  heading="Privacy policy"
>
  <p>
    This website is run by {site.company} ("we", "us"), a company based in British Columbia, Canada. {site.name} is one of
    our services. This policy explains, in plain language, what information we collect from visitors to this website, why,
    and what choices you have.
  </p>

  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We collect as little as possible.</li>
    <li>This website does not use advertising cookies or tracking cookies.</li>
    <li>We only get your name or email if you request a scorecard, book a call or email us.</li>
    <li>We only send marketing emails if you tick the box asking for them, and you can unsubscribe at any time.</li>
    <li>We do not sell personal information.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Website analytics.</strong> We may use a privacy-friendly analytics tool that does not use cookies and does not
    identify individual visitors. It tells us things like how many people visited a page, which country they were in, and
    which buttons were clicked (for example, the booking button or the newsletter link). We use this to understand whether
    the website is useful.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Booking a call.</strong> If you book a free visibility check, you are taken to a third-party booking tool. It
    collects the details you enter, such as your name, email, business name and the time you choose. We use these details
    to hold the call and follow up with you about it. The booking tool has its own privacy policy, which applies when you
    use it.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Requesting a scorecard.</strong> If you ask for a free visibility scorecard, we collect your business name, your
    city or neighbourhood, what your business does and your email address. We use these details to prepare the scorecard
    from publicly available information about your business and to email it to you. We will only send you marketing
    emails if you tick the optional box on the form. We keep a record of that choice, and every marketing email includes
    an unsubscribe link.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Emailing us.</strong> If you email us, we receive your email address and whatever you choose to write. We use it
    to reply and to keep a record of our conversation.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Your currency choice.</strong> If you switch between CAD and USD prices, your browser remembers that choice on
    your own device (in local storage). It is not sent to us and it is not a cookie.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Hosting.</strong> Our hosting provider processes technical information that every website needs to work, such
    as your IP address and browser type, to deliver pages and protect against abuse.
  </p>

  <h2>What we do not collect</h2>
  <p>
    We do not ask for or collect health information on this website. Please do not send us any information about your
    patients or clients.
  </p>

  <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
  <p>
    We share information only with the service providers we need to run this website and our business: our hosting and
    analytics provider, our booking tool and our email provider. They may only use the information to provide their service
    to us. We may also disclose information if the law requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>Where your information is stored</h2>
  <p>
    Some of the tools we use are run by companies based in the United States, and they may store or process information
    there or in other countries. That means the information may be accessible to courts and law enforcement in those
    countries under their laws.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <p>
    We keep booking and email details for as long as we need them to respond to you and to run our business, and then we
    delete them. You can ask us to delete your information sooner.
  </p>

  <h2>Your choices and rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what personal information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it. You can also
    withdraw your consent to us contacting you at any time. To do any of this, contact us using the details below. If you
    are in Canada and are not satisfied with our answer, you can contact the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada
    or the privacy commissioner for your province.
  </p>

  <h2>For visitors in the United States</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell personal information, and we do not share it for cross-context behavioural advertising. Depending on the
    state you live in, you may have the right to know what personal information we hold about you, to correct it and to
    have it deleted, and the right not to be treated differently for using these rights. To make a request, contact us
    using the details below. This website is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect their
    information.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>If we change this policy, we will post the new version on this page and update the date at the top.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about privacy? Contact the person responsible for privacy at {site.company}:
    {CONTACT_EMAIL ? <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> : <strong>{contact}</strong>}.
  </p>
</Legal>
